UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventelevatedarchitectureonthedouble25608-20260613@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260613
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Elevated Architecture on the Double
DESCRIPTION:ELEVATED ARCHITECTURE ON THE DOUBLE Most people walk through Downtown Frederick with absolutely no awareness of what’s happening above their own eyebrows\, which is precisely how gargoyles gain confidence. This tour aims to correct that. Many of the defining features of historic Downtown Frederick’s charming architecture are found high above the streets in upper stories\, cornices\, and spires. Maryland Double Deckers\, in partnership with Heritage Frederick\, invites you to experience Frederick’s historic buildings on the special Elevated Architecture tour. Discover beautifully preserved examples of commercial\, residential\, religious\, and public buildings displaying major American and European styles that span more than two centuries. Along the way\, we’ll explore how the history of Frederick is told by the enduring structures that witnessed it. DURATION: 1 hour 30 minutes DEPARTS FROM: Heritage Frederick\, 24 E Church St\, Frederick\, MD 21701
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/elevated-architecture-on-the-double/25608/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventmonocacybattlefieldtour26177-20261004@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Monocacy Battlefield Tour
DESCRIPTION:The Battle that Saved Washington Battlefields have a remarkable habit of looking peaceful. You’d never guess they were once full of people making spectacularly bad days for one another. On July 9\, 1864\, Monocacy National Battlefield became the setting for the battle remembered as the “Battle That Saved Washington.” By delaying the Confederate advance on the nation’s capital\, the Union forces bought precious time for Washington’s defenses\, making Monocacy one of the Civil War’s most significant\, and perhaps most underestimated\, battlefields. Beginning at the Monocacy Battlefield Visitor Center\, we’ll journey through the battlefield with a National Park Service guide who brings the battlefield to life.\, following the course of the fighting while uncovering the stories of the soldiers who fought here and the families whose homes suddenly found themselves in the middle of history. With an expert guide bringing the landscape to life\, you’ll discover how a quiet stretch of Maryland came to play an extraordinary role in the nation’s story. History happened here in a single day. The consequences took rather longer. DURATION: 1 hour DEPARTS FROM: Monocacy National Battlefield\, 5201 Urbana Pike Frederick\, MD 21704 TICKETING DETAILS: $35 per person. A minimum total of 15 tickets must be sold for the tour to run. If we don’t sell the required minimum of tickets\, we’ll gladly refund your purchase or credit it toward another exciting tour. We’re committed to ensuring you have a fantastic experience\, and we appreciate your understanding as we work to create fun\, unforgettable events together!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/monocacy-battlefield-tour/26177/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventwelcometoquarantinos26277-20261101@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Welcome to Quarantino's
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Quarantino's is a BRAND-NEW\, riotous musical comedy set in the heart of the pandemic. A failing local dive bar and its inept staff navigate their final day before it closes as a COVID casualty\, all while dealing with overwrought regulars\, oversexed bartenders\, and an overzealous health inspector. Irreverent\, ridiculous\, and with a lot of heart\, W2Q's will have you laughing\, humming\, and reminiscing about a time that seems both immeasurably distant and like it just happened yesterday.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/welcome-to-quarantinos/26277/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventholidaymarketkickoff26332-20261105@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Holiday Market Kickoff
DESCRIPTION:Mark your calendar and come get into the spirit of the season with our first holiday market\, November 5th-8th. We’re stringing lights\, trimming trees\, and turning our two-story dairy barn into a beautiful winter wonderland! Thursday\, November 5th will be a special evening market from 4:00pm to 8:00pm. Come enjoy the barn lit at night and get first dibs on vintage Christmas and curated holiday decor. Miku permanent jewelry\, Celebration Cellars Winery\, and Finch and Fennel will be helping us kick off the holidays! HOLIDAY KICKOFF MARKET November 5th 4:00pm to 8:00pm November 6th 10:00am to 4:00pm November 7th 10:00am to 4:00pm November 8th 10:00am to 4:00pm
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/holiday-market-kickoff/26332/
END:VEVENT
