UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventholidaybazaaratblackanklevineyards24471-20261107@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Holiday Bazaar at Black Ankle Vineyards
DESCRIPTION:Black Ankle Vineyards’ 5th Annual Holiday Bazaar is a festive\, two-weekend holiday market featuring a variety of local artisans\, makers\, and small businesses. The event brings together a thoughtfully curated selection of vendors offering unique\, handmade\, and locally sourced gifts (plus we've got some excellent bakers joining us this year). Guests can browse one-of-a-kind treasures\, enjoy Black Ankle wines\, and experience the warmth of the holiday season in a cozy vineyard setting. The Holiday Bazaar celebrates local craftsmanship\, community\, and the joy of shopping small during the holiday season.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/holiday-bazaar-at-black-ankle-vineyards/24471/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgevent94thannualbrunswickveteransday11531-20261108@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:94th Annual Brunswick Veterans Day 
DESCRIPTION:Join the Brunswick community on Sunday\, November 8\, 2026\, for our annual Veterans Day Parade\, a meaningful tradition honoring those who have served our nation. This year’s event will also recognize America’s 250th Anniversary\, adding special significance to the day. The celebration will begin with an Opening Ceremony at 1:00 PM\, followed by the Veterans Day Parade stepping off at 2:00 PM. Community members are invited to line the parade route and take part in this tribute of gratitude\, remembrance\, and patriotism.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/94th-annual-brunswick-veterans-day/11531/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventcelebrating40yearsofwinemakinginfrederickcounty26264-20261108@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Celebrating 40 Years of Wine Making in Frederick County
DESCRIPTION:Frederick County is home to three of Maryland's oldest wineries\, each with a legacy dating back to the 1970s and 1980s. Join the families behind Elk Run Vineyards\, Loew Vineyards\, and Linganore Winecellars for an afternoon of conversation. Together\, they'll reflect on 50 years of grape growing and winemaking in Frederick County\, sharing the stories that shaped Maryland's wine industry. Hear firsthand about the triumphs\, challenges\, innovations\, and unexpected moments of collaboration that have defined these pioneering wineries. Hosted by Melissa Aellen\, Director of Winery Operations for Linganore.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/celebrating-40-years-of-wine-making-in-frederick-county/26264/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfrederickcitymarket11348-20261108@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Frederick City Market
DESCRIPTION:The Frederick City Market is a local food and artisan market located in the historic district of Downtown Frederick\, Maryland. Join us on every Sunday from May through November. Parking is free on Sundays and there are usually plenty of spots on 7th Street and Market Street. You can park at Gravel and Grind (15 E 6th Street) and walk through the gap into the market lot.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/frederick-city-market/11348/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfrederickweddingsexpo9147-20261108@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Frederick Weddings Expo
DESCRIPTION:PLANNING YOUR DREAM WEDDING? START HERE! Recently engaged? Deep into wedding planning? Or maybe you’ve got the ring and have absolutely no idea what comes next? The 2026 Frederick Weddings Expo is bringing everything you need to plan the big day together under one roof! Join us Sunday\, November 8 from 12–2:30 PM at the Frederick Fairgrounds and meet local wedding professionals ready to help turn your ideas into the celebration you’ve been dreaming about. From venues and flowers to photography\, transportation\, fashion\, food\, travel and more — this is your chance to explore your options\, ask questions and make real progress on your wedding plans. Don’t miss the Walk Around Fashion Show from K&B Bridals Hagerstown\, stop by the Ring Selfie Station sponsored by Colonial Jewelers\, and get there early — the first 100 brides receive an exclusive Frederick Weddings bag and champagne glass! PLUS — NEW THIS YEAR: “LET’S TALK WEDDINGS!” Once you’ve explored the Expo\, stick around at 2:30 PM for the Wedding Forum\, where a panel of local wedding pros will answer your questions about budgets\, venues\, flowers\, food\, photography\, transportation\, travel and everything in between. The expert panel features Sarah Rosier of Sleeping Bee Designs\, Brodie Ledford of Brodie Ledford Studios\, Len Joseph of On the Town Limousines\, Rene Bonde Shiffler of Blossom & Basket Boutique\, Cory Albaugh of Burnside Events and Noelle Celeste of WorldTravel Service. Seats for the Wedding Forum are limited\, so registration is strongly encouraged!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/frederick-weddings-expo/9147/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventusairforceconcertband20985-20261108@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261108T163636Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:U.S. Air Force Concert Band
DESCRIPTION:Experience the power and precision of the United States Air Force’s premier symphonic wind ensemble. Featuring 52 active-duty musicians\, the U.S. Air Force Concert Band delivers an inspiring program of classical masterpieces\, contemporary works\, popular favorites\, and patriotic tributes. Known for musical excellence and innovation\, the ensemble regularly premieres new compositions and collaborates with top artists and institutions around the world\, reaching six million listeners at over five thousand live and televised performances each year. Join us for a stirring evening that honors their service and celebrates the unifying force of music. Learn more about The United States Air Force Bands on their official website. This show is part of the Weinberg Center’s LIVE! Series\, celebrating iconic music and exceptional musicianship. The Weinberg Center\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers a historic backdrop and excellent acoustics for a memorable concert experience.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/u-s-air-force-concert-band/20985/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
