SUMMARY:HCWHA Annual Year-in-Review: Clandestine Tales from the Heritage Area
DESCRIPTION:Calling all sleuths! You’re invited to the Heart of the Civil War Heritage Area’s Annual Year-in-Review on Monday\, November 9 from 6:00-8:00 pm at the Carriage House Inn (200 S Seton Ave\, Emmitsburg\, MD 21727). From 6:00-7:00 pm\, enjoy a mixer with heavy hors d’oeuvres and local craft beverages including signature Pumpkin “Spy”ce Martinis and Mock-tinis! From 7:00-8:00 pm\, join us for the main program featuring “Clandestine Tales from the Heritage Area.” The HCWHA Year-in-Review is generously sponsored by Visit Frederick\, with additional support provided by the Frederick County U.S. Semiquincentennial Commission. If you’d like to attend this evening of good eats and espionage with the HCWHA\, please register at the link.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/hcwha-annual-year-in-review%3a-clandestine-tales-from-the-heritage-area/26241/
